The left-hand probability exceeds $0.5$, so $68$ is above the mean. The table gives $z=2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{region}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[region] (-3.5,0) -- plot[domain=-3.5:2,samples=70,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.5:3.5,samples=90,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-3.7,0)--(3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,dashed] (2,0)--(2,{2.5*exp(-2)});
\draw[black] (0,0)--(0,-0.12);
\path (0,-0.12) node[below] {$\mu$} (2,-0.12) node[below] {$68$} (0,1) node {$0.9772$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}z&=\frac{x-\mu}{\sigma}\\2&=\frac{68-\mu}{7}\\14&=68-\mu\\\mu&=54\end{aligned}$
The mean is $54$, below $68$ as required.

The lower-tail probability is $0.0013$, so the cutoff is below the mean. By symmetry, look up its complement.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}1-0.0013\\&=0.9987\end{aligned}$
The table gives $z=-3$ at $240$ mL.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{region}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[region] (-4,0) -- plot[domain=-4:-3,samples=40,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (-3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-4:4,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4.2,0)--(4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black] (-3,0)--(-3,-0.12) (0,0)--(0,-0.12);
\path (-3,-0.12) node[below] {$240$} (0,-0.12) node[below] {$\mu$} (-3.1,0.9) node {$0.0013$} (1.5,-0.65) node {Volume (mL)};
\draw[black,->] (-3.1,0.65)--(-3.45,0.04);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}-3&=\frac{240-\mu}{3}\\-9&=240-\mu\\\mu&=249\end{aligned}$
Set the mean to $249$ mL. The cutoff is three standard deviations below this mean.

Convert to a left-hand probability.
$\begin{aligned}P(X<72)&=1-0.9332\\&=0.0668\end{aligned}$
Since this is below $0.5$, the cutoff lies below the mean. Symmetry and the table give $z=-1.5$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{region}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[region] (-1.5,0) -- plot[domain=-1.5:3.5,samples=70,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3.5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.5:3.5,samples=90,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-3.7,0)--(3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,dashed] (-1.5,0)--(-1.5,{2.5*exp(-1.125)});
\draw[black] (0,0)--(0,-0.12);
\path (-1.5,-0.12) node[below] {$72$} (0,-0.12) node[below] {$\mu$} (0.5,1) node {$0.9332$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}-1.5&=\frac{72-\mu}{12}\\-18&=72-\mu\\\mu&=90\end{aligned}$
The mean is $90$. Most values exceed $72$, consistent with the given probability.

(a) The cutoff is below the mean, so $z$ is negative. Since $1-0.0668=0.9332$, the table gives $z=-1.5$.
$\begin{aligned}-1.5&=\frac{48-60}{\sigma}\\-1.5\sigma&=-12\\\sigma&=8\end{aligned}$

(b) Convert the right-hand probability to a left-hand probability.
$\begin{aligned}P(X<80)&=1-0.0062\\&=0.9938\end{aligned}$
The cutoff is above the mean, and the table gives $z=2.5$.
$\begin{aligned}2.5&=\frac{80-60}{\sigma}\\2.5\sigma&=20\\\sigma&=8\end{aligned}$
Both standard deviations are positive. The solution sketches show the two given tails.
