The lower-tail area is $0.05$. Use inverse normal with area $0.05$, mean $0$ and standard deviation $1$ to obtain $z\approx-1.644853627$. Retain the full calculator value.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{region}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[region] (-3.5,0) -- plot[domain=-3.5:-1.644853627,samples=50,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (-1.644853627,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.5:3.5,samples=90,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.5*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-3.7,0)--(3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,dashed] (-1.644853627,0)--(-1.644853627,{2.5*exp(-1.644853627*1.644853627/2)});
\draw[black] (0,0)--(0,-0.12);
\path (-1.644853627,-0.12) node[below] {$27$} (0,-0.12) node[below] {$32$} (-2.6,1.2) node {$0.05$} (1.5,-0.65) node {Life (hours)};
\draw[black,->] (-2.6,0.95)--(-2.3,0.12);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}z&=\frac{27-32}{\sigma}\\\sigma&=\frac{-5}{z}\\\sigma&\approx3.0398\end{aligned}$
To one decimal place, $\sigma=3.0$ hours. Both the score difference and $z$ are negative, giving a positive standard deviation.
